  {"date": "2000-06-09", "venue": "On Air East", "city": "Shibuya City", "state": "Tokyo", "gap": 1, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "The Squirming Coil", "in": ">", "next": "Meatstick", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-06-13", "venue": "Club Quattro", "city": "Naka Ward", "state": "Aichi", "gap": 3, "set": "2", "next": "Wolfman's Brother", "xprev": "Weekapaug Groove", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-06-15", "venue": "Big Cat", "city": "Chuo Ward", "state": "Osaka", "gap": 2, "set": "e", "xprev": "You Enjoy Myself", "last": 1, "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-06-22", "venue": "AmSouth Amphitheatre", "city": "Antioch", "state": "TN", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Swift and high-energy playing throughout. A clean, linear build in energy, from patient and quiet interplay between Page and Trey at the beginning, building with whale call bends and rotary swirl, finally ascending to a heavenly peak. Very happy and massive hose during the peak; spacey jam on the back end -> to \"2001.\"", "out": ">", "next": "Also Sprach Zarathustra", "xprev": "Chalk Dust Torture", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-06-25", "venue": "ALLTEL Pavilion at Walnut Creek", "city": "Raleigh", "state": "NC", "gap": 3, "set": "2", "out": ">", "next": "Fast Enough for You", "xprev": "Split Open and Melt", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-06-28", "venue": "PNC Bank Arts Center", "city": "Holmdel", "state": "NJ", "gap": 1, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Another strong summer '00 straightforward \"Gotta Jibboo,\" which ebbs and flows like the best of them. Tightly played, and the band doesn't hold back anything from its bag of tricks.", "out": ">", "prev": "Harry Hood", "in": ">", "next": "When the Circus Comes", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-07-01", "venue": "Meadows Music Theatre", "city": "Hartford", "state": "CT", "gap": 3, "set": "2", "note": "Additional lyrics that referenced Chris Kuroda and Brad Sands.", "next": "Bug", "xprev": "Split Open and Melt", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-07-04", "venue": "E Centre", "city": "Camden", "state": "NJ", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The longest and most expansive \"Gotta Jibboo\" to date. At first, there is standard \"Jibboo\" tension-release playing, followed by a passage of rhythmic complexity propelled by Fish's wood blocks. This section eventually shifts to a celebratory hose passage which culminates in a breathtaking peak; this devoloves into dissonant and chaotic jazz that would feel at home in '95, which -> \"Saw It Again.\"", "out": "->", "next": "Saw It Again", "xprev": "Julius", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-07-07", "venue": "Star Lake Amphitheatre", "city": "Burgettstown", "state": "PA", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "prev": "Ghost", "in": "->", "next": "Split Open and Melt", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-07-10", "venue": "Deer Creek Music Center", "city": "Noblesville", "state": "IN", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "out": ">", "next": "Sand", "xprev": "David Bowie", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-07-14", "venue": "Polaris Amphitheater", "city": "Columbus", "state": "OH", "gap": 3, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "While shorter, this one has a stronger peak than most with lots of classic Trey/Page interplay - definitely a top-shelf \"Gotta Jibboo.\"", "out": ">", "prev": "Timber (Jerry the Mule)", "next": "Boogie On Reggae Woman", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-07-17", "venue": "KLRU Studios, University of Texas", "city": "Austin", "state": "TX", "gap": 2, "set": "1", "prev": "Beauty of My Dreams", "next": "Piper", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-09-09", "venue": "Pepsi Arena", "city": "Albany", "state": "NY", "gap": 2, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Gorgeous Trey/Page interplay in the beginning of the jam; a nice, clean, somewhat straightforward build to a massive but abbreviated peak.", "out": ">", "next": "The Curtain", "xprev": "Run Like an Antelope", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-09-15", "venue": "Hersheypark Stadium", "city": "Hershey", "state": "PA", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "prev": "First Tube", "next": "Corinna", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-09-20", "venue": "Riverbend Music Center", "city": "Cincinnati", "state": "OH", "gap": 3, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Pure, unadulterated, straight-on HOSE!!! This one is for fans of the standard \"Gotta Jibboo\" vamp-based jamming, that just continues to peak with swirling intensity.", "out": ">", "prev": "Wolfman's Brother", "next": "Mike's Song", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-09-25", "venue": "Sandstone Amphitheatre", "city": "Bonner Springs", "state": "KS", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "out": ">", "next": "Mike's Song", "xprev": "Julius", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2000-10-04", "venue": "Coors Amphitheatre", "city": "Chula Vista", "state": "CA", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "prev": "Sample in a Jar", "next": "Bug", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2003-02-20", "venue": "Allstate Arena", "city": "Rosemont", "state": "IL", "gap": 12, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Hot on the heels of an 18-minute \"Simple,\" this nearly-20 minute offering surprises, to close out set 1. A classic tension-release \"Jibboo\" gets accented with melodic blues work, before highly rhythmic Fishman fills push Trey to explore the classic hard-edged, uncompressed 2.0 tone, propelled by Page's complex chord work.", "prev": "Simple", "xnext": "Tweezer", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2003-07-29", "venue": "Post-Gazette Pavilion at Star Lake", "city": "Burgettstown", "state": "PA", "gap": 24, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Despite \"Gotta Jibboo's\" rarity in 2.0, it remained a consistently strong offering when appearing in shows. This version always feels like it's about to peak, but the band continues to push the jam forward and deeper at each turn, offering variety to create a more complex \"Jibboo\" than meets the ear.", "prev": "Camel Walk", "next": "Cool It Down", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2003-12-28", "venue": "American Airlines Arena", "city": "Miami", "state": "FL", "gap": 9, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "This one has everything to love about a good \"Gotta Jibboo\" jam - gorgeous Page/Trey interplay, a nice steady climb to the heavens, a massive peak that just plateaus and stays at the happy place, and whale call Trey delivers the icing on the cake. Sizable celebratory hose peaking towards the back half of the jam.", "next": "Suzy Greenberg", "xprev": "Tweezer Reprise", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2004-04-16", "venue": "Thomas & Mack Center", "city": "Las Vegas", "state": "NV", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Sloppy and takes time to peak, but when the band finally comes together and eventually peaks it's a gorgeous moment of clarity that cuts through everything and makes things happy for a minute, before getting goregously goopy and grimy like only '04 can.", "next": "Twist", "xprev": "Taste", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2004-06-19", "venue": "Saratoga Performing Arts Center", "city": "Saratoga Springs", "state": "NY", "gap": 4, "set": "2", "note": "Unfinished", "out": ">", "prev": "Piper", "in": "->", "next": "Limb By Limb", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2004-08-14", "venue": "Newport State Airport", "city": "Coventry", "state": "VT", "gap": 11, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The yang to 4/16/04's yin. Tight playing for '04. Dark and grimy up front, but once it pushes through to the heavens this \"Gotta Jibboo\" is breathtaking.", "prev": "Runaway Jim", "in": "->", "next": "You Enjoy Myself", "nb": 1},
